{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersets\/replacingaregistry"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Move a central list of event types, routes or registrations onto declarations that find"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"themselves."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/UniqueKeys","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/Performance"],"anchor":"Guides"}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"LinkerSets"}],"title":"Replacing a hand-written registry","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A registry is a list someone has to keep in step with the code: every analytics event type in an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array, every route in a table, every dependency registered in one function at startup. A new type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that isn’t added works everywhere except where the list is read, and nothing tells you. Moving the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"list onto LinkerSets takes four steps, and the list is deleted at the end."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Take an analytics library whose events are types conforming to ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsEvent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", collected by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hand so the library can validate their schemas at launch:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["public protocol AnalyticsEvent {","    static var name: String { get }","}","","\/\/ Every module's events, listed by hand.","let allEvents: [any AnalyticsEvent.Type] = [","    Login.self,","    Logout.self,","    PurchaseCompleted.self,","]"],"syntax":"swift"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"1. Give the library a macro","anchor":"1-Give-the-library-a-macro"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Pick a kind (“evnt” is ","type":"text"},{"code":"0x6576_6E74","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","isActive":true},{"text":" explains) and add a compiler plugin","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whose macro requires the protocol, so its records hold ","type":"text"},{"code":"any AnalyticsEvent.Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["public enum EventMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x6576_6E74 }  \/\/ \"evnt\"","","    public static func requiredConformance(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> TypeSyntax? {","        \"Analytics.AnalyticsEvent\"","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The library declares the macro and the kind, re-exports LinkerSets for the expansion, and reads"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the set for its users:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["@_exported import LinkerSets","","extension LinkerSetKind {","    static let events = LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x6576_6E74)  \/\/ \"evnt\"","}","","@attached(peer)","public macro Event() = #externalMacro(module: \"AnalyticsMacros\", type: \"EventMacro\")","","public enum AnalyticsEvents {","    public static var all: [any AnalyticsEvent.Type] {","        LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>(kind: .events).values","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The re-export is required. The expansion lands in each user’s file and calls LinkerSets’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"#linkerSetRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" there, so that file must see the LinkerSets module. A library that imports"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"LinkerSets without re-exporting it leaves its users’ files failing with “no macro named"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"‘linkerSetRecord’” unless each one imports LinkerSets too. The re-export also puts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSet"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSetKind"},{"type":"text","text":" in scope wherever the library is imported. Keep the kind"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"internal and hand users the values through the library’s own API ("},{"code":"AnalyticsEvents.all","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), so the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"set is read in one place."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The LinkerSetsMacroSupport module’s documentation has the package targets this needs."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"2. Read the set beside the list","anchor":"2-Read-the-set-beside-the-list"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Before touching any event, read both and compare them, in a test or a debug build:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let discovered = AnalyticsEvents.all","let missing = allEvents.filter { listed in !discovered.contains { $0 == listed } }"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"missing","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" starts as the whole list and shrinks as events are marked.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"3. Mark each event where it’s declared","anchor":"3-Mark-each-event-where-its-declared"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["@Event","struct Login: AnalyticsEvent {","    static let name = \"login\"","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An event that doesn’t conform fails to compile. A generic event type, or one nested in a generic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type, is refused with a message, as "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse"},{"type":"text","text":" lists; such a type needs its concrete"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specializations listed by hand, or a concrete wrapper."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"4. Delete the list","anchor":"4-Delete-the-list"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Once ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"missing"},{"text":" is empty, the library reads the set instead:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let allEvents = LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>(kind: .events).values"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"and the hand-written array goes. A new event is registered by writing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":" on it, in whichever"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"module declares it."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Other registries","anchor":"Other-registries"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The same steps fit any list whose entries can be declared as constants, functions or types:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Routes"}]},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Route static let profile = Route(path: \"\/profile\")"},{"type":"text","text":", read as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSet<Route>"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Migrations","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"code":"@Migration static func addUsers(_ db: inout Database)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", read as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"LinkerSet<(inout Database) -> Void>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", sorted by a version the migration declares."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Dependency registrations","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"code":"@Registration static func register(_ container: Container)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"module registering its own factories, read and called once at startup."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A registry whose order matters gets it from the entries, never from the set: the linker’s order is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stable but not one you choose ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/WhatTheMacrosRefuse":{"role":"article","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/whatthemacrosrefuse","title":"What the macros refuse","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","abstract":[{"text":"Every declaration a record can’t describe is a compile error, with a message that says why.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/PlatformsAndLinking":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where records are found, how, and which test shows it."}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/platformsandlinking","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Platforms and linking","type":"topic"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/UniqueKeys":{"type":"topic","title":"Unique keys","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Make two records of one kind with the same key fail to build, within one executable or library."}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/uniquekeys","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/UniqueKeys","role":"article"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/Performance":{"type":"topic","title":"Performance","abstract":[{"text":"What records cost as an app grows: nothing at launch, a walk of the records when a set is read,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and a few milliseconds of build time per marked declaration.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/performance","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/Performance","role":"article"},"doc://LinkerSetsRuntime/documentation/LinkerSetsRuntime/LinkerSet":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsruntime\/linkerset","kind":"symbol","title":"LinkerSet","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSet","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every record of one kind, across every image the program has loaded, and the values they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"produce."}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LinkerSet","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"LinkerSet","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://LinkerSetsRuntime/documentation/LinkerSetsRuntime/LinkerSetKind":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSetKind","title":"LinkerSetKind","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LinkerSetKind","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"LinkerSetKind","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tag that says which client a linker-set record belongs to."}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsruntime\/linkersetkind"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/DeclaringAKind":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","abstract":[{"text":"Pick the number that tags your declarations, and decide whether your users write it.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/declaringakind","role":"article","title":"Declaring a kind","type":"topic"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Declarations that register themselves at compile time and are found at run time across every module a program links.","type":"text"}],"title":"LinkerSets","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets","role":"collection"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/FindingRecords":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Read every declaration of a kind, as the type you expect."}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/findingrecords","role":"article","title":"Finding records","type":"topic"}}}